    "content": "Turn your own photos into viral rap duo videos with [Photo to Rap AI Online](/) in 3 minutes.\n\nA great rap duo is more than two good rappers. It is chemistry: two voices that finish each other's lines, one who sets up and one who knocks it down, or a rapper and a producer who build one sound. Here are 15 of the best rap duos in hip-hop history, roughly by era, with the record to start with.\n\n\n\n## The list\n\n\n\n| Duo | Members | From | Start with |\n| Eric B. & Rakim | Eric B., Rakim | Long Island, New York | *Paid in Full* (1987) |\n| DJ Jazzy Jeff & The Fresh Prince | DJ Jazzy Jeff, Will Smith | Philadelphia | \"Parents Just Don't Understand\" (1988) |\n| EPMD | Erick Sermon, Parrish Smith | Brentwood, New York | *Strictly Business* (1988) |\n| Gang Starr | Guru, DJ Premier | Brooklyn, New York | *Moment of Truth* (1998) |\n| Pete Rock & CL Smooth | Pete Rock, CL Smooth | Mount Vernon, New York | \"They Reminisce Over You (T.R.O.Y.)\" (1992) |\n| Kris Kross | Chris Kelly, Chris Smith | Atlanta | \"Jump\" (1992) |\n| UGK | Bun B, Pimp C | Port Arthur, Texas | \"Int'l Players Anthem\" (2007) |\n| 8Ball & MJG | 8Ball, MJG | Memphis | *Comin' Out Hard* (1993) |\n| OutKast | André 3000, Big Boi | Atlanta | *Aquemini* (1998) |\n| Mobb Deep | Prodigy, Havoc | Queensbridge, New York | *The Infamous* (1995) |\n| Black Star | Mos Def (Yasiin Bey), Talib Kweli | Brooklyn | *Mos Def & Talib Kweli Are Black Star* (1998) |\n| Method Man & Redman | Method Man, Redman | Staten Island and Newark | *Blackout!* (1999) |\n| Clipse | Pusha T, Malice | Virginia Beach | \"Grindin'\" (2002) |\n| Run the Jewels | El-P, Killer Mike | Brooklyn and Atlanta | *Run the Jewels 2* (2014) |\n| Rae Sremmurd | Swae Lee, Slim Jxmmi | Tupelo, Mississippi | \"Black Beatles\" (2016) |\n\n\n\n## What makes them work\n\n\n**The rapper and the DJ.** Eric B. & Rakim, Gang Starr and Pete Rock & CL Smooth are the classic setup: one voice, one producer, one sound you can recognize in two bars. Rakim's calm, internal-rhyme flow over Eric B.'s beats changed how people rapped.\n\n\n**The two voices that trade.** OutKast, UGK, Mobb Deep, Clipse and Run the Jewels are two rappers who pass the mic back and forth. OutKast's *Speakerboxxx/The Love Below* won the Grammy for Album of the Year in 2004, still one of the few rap albums to do it.\n\n\n**The brothers.** Clipse (Pusha T and Malice) and Rae Sremmurd (Swae Lee and Slim Jxmmi) are brothers, and it shows in how tight the back-and-forth is. \"Black Beatles\" went to No. 1 on the Billboard Hot 100 in 2016.\n\n\n**The firsts.** DJ Jazzy Jeff & The Fresh Prince won the first Grammy ever given for a rap performance, for \"Parents Just Don't Understand\" (1989 ceremony). Kris Kross's \"Jump\" spent eight weeks at No. 1 in 1992.\n\n\n\n## Honorable mention: Unc & Phew\n\n\nQuavo and Takeoff of Migos, uncle and nephew, recorded as the duo **Unc & Phew** in 2022. Their single \"Hotel Lobby (Unc & Phew)\" and its orange-booth performance became the Hotel Lobby AI trend in 2026. The full story is in [Quavo and Takeoff: Unc & Phew explained](/blog/quavo-and-takeoff).\n\n\n\n## Make your own rap duo\n\n\nEvery duo above started with two people and a mic. You can put yourself and a friend, a partner or a sibling in a rap duo video from two photos: the [[Photo to Rap AI](/) studio](/) writes an **original** rap and beat about whatever you choose and renders the two of you performing it, lip-synced, in about 3 minutes. It doesn't use any real artist's song or clone anyone's voice.\n\n\nFor songs about the friendship itself, see [rap songs about friends](/blog/rap-songs-about-friends). Need a name first? Try the [rap duo name generator](/rap-duo-name-generator). Want the viral look? Pick the orange booth on the [Hotel Lobby AI](/hotel-lobby-ai) page, or see [how to make an AI rap video](/blog/how-to-make-an-ai-rap-video) step by step.\n\n\n\n## FAQ\n\n\n**Who is the best rap duo of all time?** OutKast is the most common answer: a string of classic albums, a Grammy Album of the Year and two very different voices that fit. Eric B. & Rakim, UGK and Mobb Deep are the usual picks right behind them.\n\n\n**What are some female rap duos?** City Girls (Yung Miami and JT) from Miami are the best-known female rap duo of recent years, with hits like \"Act Up\" (2018).\n\n\n**What is a rap duet?** A song where two rappers share the track, trading verses or lines. Rap duos make them by default; a duet can also be a one-off between solo artists.\n\n\n**Are rap duos still a thing?** Yes: Run the Jewels and Rae Sremmurd kept the format alive in the 2010s, and the Hotel Lobby trend turned \"two people, one mic\" into something anyone can do.\n\n## Create Your Own AI Rap Video Now\nWant to turn photos of you and your friends into an authentic hip-hop clip? Head over to [Photo to Rap AI Generator](/#generator) and generate your free preview today! Also check out the iconic orange studio on [Hotel Lobby AI](/hotel-lobby-ai)."
